@@ -0,0 +1,201 @@
+---
+status: design-intent
+---
+
+# todo-check Line-Number Validation Implementation Plan
+
+**Goal:** `node scripts/todo-check.js` reports an entry citing a `path:line` past the end of its
+target file, instead of exiting 0.
+**Architecture:** Reuse `scripts/docs-check.js`'s existing `PATHISH` parser and a newly-exported
+`lineCount`, applied to `TODO.md`'s own two citation shapes — a backtick span and a markdown
+link's target — inside `todo-check.js`'s per-entry loop. No new regex, no new dependency.
+**Tech Stack:** Node.js built-ins only (`node:fs`, `node:path`), `node --test` (this repo carries
+no other test runner and no `dependencies` in `package.json`).
+**Spec:** [2026-09-25-todo-check-linecount-design.md](2026-09-25-todo-check-linecount-design.md)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- `node --test` is the only test command (`package.json` `scripts.test`); no dependency may be
+  added — `package.json` has no `dependencies` block at all.
+- `tests/` is one file per module/behaviour; a new scratch file or directory comes from
+  `tests/tmp.js`, never a hand-rolled temp path.
+- `TODO.md`'s role is `reference` (`lib/docs.js` `ROOT_REFERENCE`), already scanned by
+  `scripts/docs-check.js` for the same `path:line` convention project-wide; this task adds the
+  same check to `todo-check.js`'s own standalone run, it does not replace or duplicate
+  `docs-check.js`'s regex — three scripts already do this by requiring it:
+  `scripts/input-check.js:23`, `scripts/docs-audit.js:32`, `scripts/memory-check.js:33`.
+- No `CLAUDE.md` exists in this repository.
+
+## Task 1: todo-check validates a `path:line` citation's line number
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `scripts/docs-check.js` — export `lineCount` alongside `CODE`/`PATHISH`
+- Modify: `scripts/todo-check.js` — require `CODE`/`PATHISH`/`lineCount` from `./docs-check.js`;
+  check a backtick `path:line` span and a markdown link's `:line` suffix against the target
+  file's line count; strip a link target's `:line` suffix before the existence check
+- Modify: `TODO.md` — "enforces all nine" → "ten" with the new clause; remove the
+  `〔docs〕todo-check 不驗 path:line 的行號` bullet this task delivers
+- Test: `tests/todo-check.test.js` — three new cases
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: `docs-check.js`'s exported `CODE` (matches one backtick-delimited span, 2-120 chars),
+  `PATHISH` (matches an optional `./`, then a path, then an optional `:line` or `:line-line`;
+  capture groups 1=path, 2=start line, 3=end line), and the new `lineCount(root, rel)` →
+  `number|null`.
+- Produces: none — this is the only task.
+
+**Dispatch:** implementer, sonnet — a transcription-plus-tests change against two already-read
+files.
+
+In `scripts/docs-check.js`, at the end of the file:
+
+```js
+module.exports = { scan, report, parseArgs, resolveRef, LINK, CODE, PATHISH, external, readFile, isMarkdown, lineCount };
+```
+
+In `scripts/todo-check.js`, add near the other `require`s:
+
+```js
+const { CODE, PATHISH, lineCount } = require('./docs-check.js');
+```
+
+In `scripts/todo-check.js`, replace the `for (const target of linksIn(entry.text))` loop (the one
+checking `dead link` and `stale citation`) with:
+
+```js
+        for (const target of linksIn(entry.text)) {
+            const hit = PATHISH.exec(target);
+            const filePath = hit ? hit[1] : target;
+            const full = path.resolve(base, filePath);
+            if (!fs.existsSync(full)) {
+                problems.push({
+                    line: entry.line,
+                    kind: 'dead link',
+                    detail: target + ' does not exist. Either the entry is finished and should be removed, or the detail moved.',
+                });
+                continue;
+            }
+            if (hit && hit[2]) {
+                const wanted = parseInt(hit[2], 10);
+                const wantedEnd = hit[3] ? parseInt(hit[3], 10) : null;
+                const n = lineCount(base, filePath);
+                const label = filePath + ':' + wanted + (wantedEnd ? '-' + wantedEnd : '');
+                if (n !== null && (wantedEnd || wanted) > n) {
+                    problems.push({
+                        line: entry.line,
+                        kind: 'past end',
+                        detail: label + ' but the file ends at ' + n,
+                    });
+                }
+            }
+            const role = docs.roleOf(tree, path.relative(base, full));
+            if (STALE_ROLES.includes(role)) {
+                problems.push({
+                    line: entry.line,
+                    kind: 'stale citation',
+                    detail: target + ' is filed as ' + role + ', a role that records a moment rather than the present. Point at the code this is about, or at a reference page.',
+                });
+            }
+        }
+
+        CODE.lastIndex = 0;
+        let codeHit;
+        while ((codeHit = CODE.exec(entry.text)) !== null) {
+            const hit = PATHISH.exec(codeHit[1].trim());
+            if (!hit || !hit[2]) continue;
+            const ref = hit[1];
+            const full = path.resolve(base, ref);
+            if (!fs.existsSync(full)) continue;
+            const wanted = parseInt(hit[2], 10);
+            const wantedEnd = hit[3] ? parseInt(hit[3], 10) : null;
+            const n = lineCount(base, ref);
+            const label = ref + ':' + wanted + (wantedEnd ? '-' + wantedEnd : '');
+            if (n !== null && (wantedEnd || wanted) > n) {
+                problems.push({
+                    line: entry.line,
+                    kind: 'past end',
+                    detail: label + ' but the file ends at ' + n,
+                });
+            }
+        }
+    }
+```
+
+(The closing `}` on the last line closes the `for (const entry of found)` loop already in the
+file — this block replaces everything from the existing `for (const target of linksIn(...))` line
+through its own closing brace, one level up from that loop's `}`.)
+
+In `TODO.md`, line 55, replace:
+
+```md
+`node scripts/todo-check.js` enforces all nine: a link that no longer resolves is
+an entry someone forgot to close, a link that still resolves but points at a
+```
+
+with, still in `TODO.md`:
+
+```md
+`node scripts/todo-check.js` enforces all ten: a link that no longer resolves is
+an entry someone forgot to close, a citation whose `path:line` runs past the end
+of the file it names is the same failure caught one line late, a link that still
+resolves but points at a
+```
+
+In `TODO.md`, under `## Ready`, delete this bullet entirely (the fix this task ships is what it
+describes):
+
+```md
+- 〔docs〕todo-check 不驗 `path:line` 的行號：改成不存在的行仍然 exit 0 — [scripts/todo-check.js](scripts/todo-check.js). docs-check 補得到一部分，但卡 role、引文與讀得到目標三個前提。
+```
+
+In `tests/todo-check.test.js`, add after the existing `'a link to a file that no longer exists is a dead entry'` test:
+
+```js
+test('a citation whose line number runs past the end of its file is a problem', () => {
+  const file = fixture(
+    '# TODO\n\n## Ready\n\n- see `short.js:5` for it.\n',
+    { 'short.js': 'one\ntwo\n' },
+  );
+  const { out, code } = run(file);
+  assert.equal(code, 1);
+  assert.match(out, /past end/);
+  assert.match(out, /short\.js:5 but the file ends at 2/);
+});
+
+test('a link whose target carries a line number past the end is a problem, not a dead link', () => {
+  const file = fixture(
+    '# TODO\n\n## Ready\n\n- [see](short.js:5) for it.\n',
+    { 'short.js': 'one\ntwo\n' },
+  );
+  const { out, code } = run(file);
+  assert.equal(code, 1);
+  assert.match(out, /past end/);
+  assert.doesNotMatch(out, /dead link/);
+});
+
+test('a citation whose line number is in range passes', () => {
+  const file = fixture(
+    '# TODO\n\n## Ready\n\n- see `short.js:2` and [also](short.js:1) for it.\n',
+    { 'short.js': 'one\ntwo\n' },
+  );
+  const { out, code } = run(file);
+  assert.equal(code, 0);
+  assert.doesNotMatch(out, /past end/);
+});
+```
+
+## Coverage
+
